    "alternatePackage": {
      "@id": "https://api.nuget.org/v3/catalog0/data/2026.11.04.10.26.22/linqbuilder.efcore.automapper.1.0.1.json#deprecation/alternatePackage",
      "id": "LinqBuilder.EFCore",
      "range": "*"
    },
    "message": "Discontinued in LinqBuilder v2.0.0. Its methods projected the query with AutoMapper before applying the specification, which you can do directly: install LinqBuilder.EFCore and write query.ProjectTo<T>(configuration).AnyAsync(specification), and the same for AllAsync, CountAsync, FirstAsync and the rest. If you rely on computed properties, add .DecompileAsync() from DelegateDecompiler.EntityFrameworkCore after ProjectTo, as this package did. Release notes: https://github.com/Baune8D/LinqBuilder/releases/tag/v2.0.0",
    "reasons": [
      "Legacy"
    ]
  },
  "description": "Extensions for querying EF Core with AutoMapper projections.",
